# Copy this file to .env and fill it in. Docker Compose passes these variables to the server.
# Never commit .env. This repository ignores it.
#
# The names are the ones that alexia-api.toml writes after env:. The starter file for an
# account called family uses these two. For an account called garcia the names are
# PORTAL_GARCIA_USERNAME and PORTAL_GARCIA_PASSWORD, and so on for each account.
#
# Do not start a name with ALEXIA_API_. The server reads that prefix as its own settings and
# refuses a name that is not one.
#
# Put each value in single quotes. Compose reads a $ in an unquoted value as a variable, so the
# password pa$word would reach the school as pa, and a wrong password can lock your account.
# A password that holds a single quote goes in double quotes, with \$, \" and \\ for those three
# characters.
PORTAL_FAMILY_USERNAME=''
PORTAL_FAMILY_PASSWORD=''
